#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186082954 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b0262c8-c029-5a72-846b-1b4f4f3306ba" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Quadratic Polynomial Given a Double Root and a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/id #uuid "65baa4aa-0b90-52d0-91a2-93377e13af18" :question/math-academy-id "e-5788" :question/problem "The quadratic polynomial $P(x)$ has the double root $x_1=x_2=5,$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=1.$ Find $P(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our quadratic polynomial has the double root ${\\color{black}x_1=x_2=5},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is ${\\color{black}a=1},$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})^{2} & =1\\cdot {(x-5)}^{2} \\\\  & ={(x-5)}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(x-5)}^{2} & ={x}^{2}-10x+25.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x) = x^2 - 10x+25.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186082955 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "70c149d8-3739-564c-97c5-6636860ad0c4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Quadratic Polynomial Given Two Imaginary or Complex Roots"}] :question/id #uuid "98750271-1c2d-5b5f-851c-24963da1e6bf" :question/math-academy-id "e-5789" :question/problem "The quadratic polynomial $f(z)$ with real coefficients has roots $z_1=3+\\textrm{i}$ and $z_2=3-\\textrm{i},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $2.$ Find $f(z).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our quadratic polynomial has roots ${\\color{black}z_1=3+\\textrm{i}}$ and ${\\color{black}z_2=3-\\textrm{i}},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is ${\\color{black}a=2},$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(z-{z}_{1})(z-{z}_{2}) & =2(z-(3+\\text{i}))(z-(3-\\text{i}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(z-(3+\\text{i}))(z-(3-\\text{i})) & =2({z}^{2}-(3+\\text{i})z-(3-\\text{i})z+(3+\\text{i})(3-\\text{i})) \\\\  & =2({z}^{2}-(3+\\text{i}+3-\\text{i})z+({3}^{2}-{\\text{i}}^{2})) \\\\  & =2({z}^{2}-6z+(9+1)) \\\\  & =2({z}^{2}-6z+10) \\\\  & =2{z}^{2}-12z+20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(z) = 2z^2-12z+20.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186082956 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1ee21c78-209f-564b-a005-86f58699a3be" :knowledge-point/title "Factoring a Quadratic Polynomial With Complex Roots"}] :question/id #uuid "0af567b3-a239-5149-b022-d71693c63661" :question/math-academy-id "e-5791" :question/problem "Factor $u^2-2u+10.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we let $f(u) = u^2-2u+10.$\n\nNext, we solve $f(u) = 0$ by completing the square, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(u) & =0 \\\\ {u}^{2}-2u+10 & =0 \\\\ ({u}^{2}-2u+{1}^{2})-{1}^{2}+10 & =0 \\\\ (u-1)^{2}-1+10 & =0 \\\\ (u-1)^{2}+9 & =0 \\\\ (u-1)^{2} & =-9 \\\\ (u-1)^{2} & =9{\\text{i}}^{2} \\\\ (u-1)^{2} & =(3\\text{i})^{2} \\\\ u-1 & =\\pm 3\\text{i} \\\\ u & =1\\pm 3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since our quadratic equation has roots $u_1=1+ 3\\textrm{i}$ and $u_2=1- 3\\textrm{i},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=1,$ the expression $u^2-2u+10$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{2}-2u+10 & =a(u-{u}_{1})(u-{u}_{2}) \\\\  & =(u-(1+3\\text{i}))(u-(1-3\\text{i})).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186082961 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b2478305-485c-53a6-9d6c-a72e0764dd4e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Quadratic Polynomial Given Two Real Roots and a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/id #uuid "a9e7aedc-1b2b-5fb7-b8fb-1f9ef7c0643a" :question/math-academy-id "e-5887" :question/problem "The quadratic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots $x_1=2, x_2=5,$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $3.$ Find $P(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our quadratic polynomial has roots ${\\color{black}x_1=2}$ and ${\\color{black}x_2=5},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is ${\\color{black}a=3},$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2}) & =3(x-2)(x-5) \\\\  & =3(x-2)(x-5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(x-2)(x-5) & =3({x}^{2}-7x+10) \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}-21x+30.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x) = 3x^2-21x+30.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278313 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b0262c8-c029-5a72-846b-1b4f4f3306ba" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Quadratic Polynomial Given a Double Root and a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9c7799e0-c38a-59d5-81c8-48db76d084c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9{x}^{2}+6x-12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278315} {:answer/id #uuid "02199bf7-9e3a-5585-bf0f-0ea9df1c6c30" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9{x}^{2}-6x+6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278316} {:answer/id #uuid "4a7854b8-c2cb-5989-9dec-46d0258bf5f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9{x}^{2}+12x+4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278317} {:answer/id #uuid "73b95c43-24d8-5889-be62-9f7d0626ca8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9{x}^{2}-12x+4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278318} {:answer/id #uuid "eed7dfcf-ebac-554a-ad89-ab7a2456b953" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9{x}^{2}-6x-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278319}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4a7854b8-c2cb-5989-9dec-46d0258bf5f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9{x}^{2}+12x+4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278317} :answer-field/id #uuid "085411cc-4f1c-5e5d-8088-6aa979d52a91" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278314}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6d0aac9d-6cc7-5552-8099-d9c726cdd252" :question/math-academy-id "q-104330" :question/problem "The quadratic polynomial $P(x)$ has the double root ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=-\\frac{2}{3},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=9.$ Find $P(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our quadratic polynomial has the double root ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=-\\frac{2}{3},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=9,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})^{2} & =9{(x-(-\\frac{2}{3}))}^{2} \\\\  & =9{(x+\\frac{2}{3})}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9{(x+\\frac{2}{3})}^{2} & =9({x}^{2}+\\frac{4}{3}x+\\frac{4}{9}) \\\\  & =9{x}^{2}+12x+4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=9{x}^{2}+12x+4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278320 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1ee21c78-209f-564b-a005-86f58699a3be" :knowledge-point/title "Factoring a Quadratic Polynomial With Complex Roots"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4835ca44-f161-5b50-9ee7-8517e7df6f16" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u-(3+2\\text{i})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278322} {:answer/id #uuid "8c348a10-98f0-5faa-9663-6e7c79d4d88e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u-(-1-2\\text{i})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278323} {:answer/id #uuid "87a50535-3164-557c-aa2f-a283a606d3da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u-(1+4\\text{i})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278324} {:answer/id #uuid "7431a4cb-02fa-527e-b3af-ada42c76de1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u-(2+\\text{i})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278325} {:answer/id #uuid "b3587d37-f7d2-5b1e-8197-d38b0f0bd639" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u-(1-2\\text{i})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278326}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b3587d37-f7d2-5b1e-8197-d38b0f0bd639" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u-(1-2\\text{i})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278326} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8c2880a-2437-59fa-ab3d-2a81bcf544f7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278321}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "54ac6bbc-3ef6-59e6-9f7d-2343e7a4c075" :question/math-academy-id "q-107523" :question/problem "Which of the following is a factor of ${u}^{2}-2u+5?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we let $f(u)={u}^{2}-2u+5.$\n\nNext, we solve $f(u)=0$ by completing the square, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(u) & =0 \\\\ {u}^{2}-2u+5 & =0 \\\\ ({u}^{2}-2\\cdot u+{1}^{2})-{1}^{2}+5 & =0 \\\\ (u-1)^{2}+4 & =0 \\\\ (u-1)^{2} & =-4 \\\\ (u-1)^{2} & =4{\\text{i}}^{2} \\\\ (u-1)^{2} & =(2\\text{i})^{2} \\\\ u-1 & =\\pm 2\\text{i} \\\\ u & =1\\pm 2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince our quadratic equation has roots ${u}_{1}=1+2\\text{i}$ and ${u}_{2}=1-2\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=1,$ the expression ${u}^{2}-2u+5$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{2}-2u+5 & =a(u-{u}_{1})(u-{u}_{2}) \\\\  & =(u-(1+2\\text{i}))(u-(1-2\\text{i})).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, among the given options, only $u-(1-2\\text{i})$ is a factor of ${u}^{2}-2u+5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278327 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b0262c8-c029-5a72-846b-1b4f4f3306ba" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Quadratic Polynomial Given a Double Root and a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "802b9584-bb20-55cb-8e74-930d7e4bddc4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{y}^{2}-3y+96" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278329} {:answer/id #uuid "9e4079ec-58cf-5d5a-9821-718da5c586f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{y}^{2}-12y+32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278330} {:answer/id #uuid "96dc2268-34c8-5561-a2a0-2ce38ba6accf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{y}^{2}-4y+24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278331} {:answer/id #uuid "d62d10f9-9481-5ed6-ba3c-c78fd02e0d3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{y}^{2}-24y+48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278332} {:answer/id #uuid "38da6fda-eb86-5d1b-9824-34442c3353b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{y}^{2}-8y+16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278333}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d62d10f9-9481-5ed6-ba3c-c78fd02e0d3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{y}^{2}-24y+48" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278332} :answer-field/id #uuid "e9682328-9250-599d-8be2-3c20d60571db" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278328}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "59a0c362-ff2d-5bd3-9fe0-170e7fdb2dd3" :question/math-academy-id "q-107695" :question/problem "The quadratic polynomial $P(y)$ has the double root ${y}_{1}={y}_{2}=4,$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=3.$ Find $P(y).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our quadratic polynomial has the double root ${y}_{1}={y}_{2}=4,$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=3,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(y-{y}_{1})^{2} & =3{(y-4)}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{(y-4)}^{2} & =3({y}^{2}-8y+16) \\\\  & =3{y}^{2}-24y+48.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(y)=3{y}^{2}-24y+48.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278334 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1ee21c78-209f-564b-a005-86f58699a3be" :knowledge-point/title "Factoring a Quadratic Polynomial With Complex Roots"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2aa0bb31-c2a9-5c48-abc1-add25d189cbc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z-(7-2\\text{i})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278336} {:answer/id #uuid "93326644-a9d0-528c-b9bd-403724c83c65" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z-(4-3\\text{i})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278337} {:answer/id #uuid "f5ac2d53-6247-548f-bef7-64fa1597a103" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z-(1-2\\text{i})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278338} {:answer/id #uuid "c41e3ad7-f79c-5cdc-98bb-34231a074db7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z-(3-4\\text{i})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278339} {:answer/id #uuid "a5890693-f8ae-55e3-88ab-ac6fb4664e81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z-(2-\\text{i})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278340}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "93326644-a9d0-528c-b9bd-403724c83c65" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z-(4-3\\text{i})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278337} :answer-field/id #uuid "215810b0-7b45-5570-84cf-4a000433f309" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278335}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "eb1c77ee-2f79-5f32-b270-cdcc5ae525de" :question/math-academy-id "q-107697" :question/problem "Which of the following is a factor of $3{z}^{2}-24z+75?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we let $f(z)=3{z}^{2}-24z+75.$\n\nNext, we solve $f(z)=0$ by completing the square, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(z) & =0 \\\\ 3{z}^{2}-24z+75 & =0 \\\\ {z}^{2}-8z+25 & =0 \\\\ ({z}^{2}-2\\cdot 4\\cdot z+{4}^{2})-{4}^{2}+25 & =0 \\\\ (z-4)^{2}-16+25 & =0 \\\\ (z-4)^{2}+9 & =0 \\\\ (z-4)^{2} & =-9 \\\\ (z-4)^{2} & =9{\\text{i}}^{2} \\\\ (z-4)^{2} & =(3\\text{i})^{2} \\\\ z-4 & =\\pm 3\\text{i} \\\\ z & =4\\pm 3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince our quadratic equation has roots ${z}_{1}=4+3\\text{i}$ and ${z}_{2}=4-3\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=3,$ the expression $3{z}^{2}-24z+75$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{z}^{2}-24z+75 & =a(z-{z}_{1})(z-{z}_{2}) \\\\  & =3(z-(4+3\\text{i}))(z-(4-3\\text{i})).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, among the given options, only $z-(4-3\\text{i})$ is a factor of $3{z}^{2}-24z+75.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278341 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b2478305-485c-53a6-9d6c-a72e0764dd4e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Quadratic Polynomial Given Two Real Roots and a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d513065d-9c14-5425-aeea-3995ee21b69d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3x^2+9x+30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278343} {:answer/id #uuid "e3175648-7718-5eeb-a2a8-de33dc893e58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3x^2-9x+30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278344}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e3175648-7718-5eeb-a2a8-de33dc893e58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3x^2-9x+30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278344} :answer-field/id #uuid "bfec8835-f216-5930-b0de-838ed3570de5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278342}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "77ae731a-e7b1-5d7d-a016-3032b69c72a7" :question/math-academy-id "q-275105" :question/problem "The quadratic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=2,{x}_{2}=-5,$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $-3.$ Find $P(x).$\n\n$P(x)=$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Since our quadratic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}=2$ and ${x}_{2}=-5,$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=-3,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2}) & =(-3)(x-2)(x-(-5)) \\\\  & =-3(x-2)(x+5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3(x-2)(x+5) & =-3({x}^{2}+5x-2x-10) \\\\  & =-3({x}^{2}+3x-10) \\\\  & =-3{x}^{2}-9x+30.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=-3{x}^{2}-9x+30.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278345 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "70c149d8-3739-564c-97c5-6636860ad0c4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Quadratic Polynomial Given Two Imaginary or Complex Roots"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c99ca4c-6e50-57a0-abea-7aa3d3256586" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}-16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278347} {:answer/id #uuid "e0e69f3e-7e73-5ba5-a080-06becba660d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+6x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278348} {:answer/id #uuid "15850e13-27b4-56b7-9ddf-acad6b8a765a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278349} {:answer/id #uuid "8fb81792-2508-50b0-b4c3-5843b32ea1e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}-36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278350} {:answer/id #uuid "e82f38af-2ea4-5fce-baff-aba2b3906f35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278351}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e82f38af-2ea4-5fce-baff-aba2b3906f35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278351} :answer-field/id #uuid "169fea92-0a98-5a18-862d-e0f4fa917768" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278346}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "847b083e-81ae-5df7-a482-aef291b5630a" :question/math-academy-id "q-28185" :question/problem "The quadratic polynomial $f(x)$ has real coefficients, has roots ${x}_{1}=6\\text{i}$ and ${x}_{2}=-6\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $1.$ Find $f(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our quadratic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}=6\\text{i}$ and ${x}_{2}=-6\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=1,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2}) & =(1)(x-6\\text{i})(x-(-6\\text{i})) \\\\  & =(x-6\\text{i})(x+6\\text{i})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-6\\text{i})(x+6\\text{i}) & ={x}^{2}-(6\\text{i})^{2} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}-36{\\text{i}}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}+36.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)={x}^{2}+36.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278352 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b2478305-485c-53a6-9d6c-a72e0764dd4e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Quadratic Polynomial Given Two Real Roots and a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01414e6a-64f6-51e7-910e-a137c6e15089" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^2+x-20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278354}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "01414e6a-64f6-51e7-910e-a137c6e15089" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^2+x-20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278354} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d714f5f-e8eb-584f-b65f-5aff335e240b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278353}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "82ac93a9-a71e-5418-8ea8-2d2c10682648" :question/math-academy-id "q-282069" :question/problem "The quadratic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=-5,{x}_{2}=4,$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $1.$ Find $P(x).$\n\n$P(x)=$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Since our quadratic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}=-5$ and ${x}_{2}=4,$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=1,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2}) & =(1)(x-(-5))(x-4) \\\\  & =(x+5)(x-4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+5)(x-4) & ={x}^{2}-4x+5x-20 \\\\  & ={x}^{2}+x-20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)={x}^{2}+x-20.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278355 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b0262c8-c029-5a72-846b-1b4f4f3306ba" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Quadratic Polynomial Given a Double Root and a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a1c40a6-51b9-5b4b-833e-26bc1c65e93f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9x^2-54x-81" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278357} {:answer/id #uuid "a6a8efd4-7954-5478-a98e-1b722075bc11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9x^2+54x-81" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278358}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a6a8efd4-7954-5478-a98e-1b722075bc11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-9x^2+54x-81" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278358} :answer-field/id #uuid "13b76ca6-d321-50f7-88b7-6e5404c215e4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278356}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "53935da2-c3cd-5bfa-a008-a66892a65894" :question/math-academy-id "q-282084" :question/problem "The quadratic polynomial $P(x)$ has the double root ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=3,$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=-9.$ Find $P(x).$\n\n$P(x)=$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Since our quadratic polynomial has the double root ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=3,$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=-9,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})^{2} & =(-9){(x-3)}^{2} \\\\  & =-9(x-3)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-9(x-3)^{2} & =-9({x}^{2}-6x+9) \\\\  & =-9{x}^{2}+54x-81.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=-9{x}^{2}+54x-81.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278359 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b0262c8-c029-5a72-846b-1b4f4f3306ba" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Quadratic Polynomial Given a Double Root and a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88fd2a55-335e-545a-9224-7891cf533fca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16x^2+128x+256" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278361}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "88fd2a55-335e-545a-9224-7891cf533fca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16x^2+128x+256" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278361} :answer-field/id #uuid "ab298844-eadf-5699-8f27-153cda985b42" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278360}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "92f379ad-bc52-54c7-9314-d46129849845" :question/math-academy-id "q-282122" :question/problem "The quadratic polynomial $P(x)$ has the double root ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=-4,$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=16.$ Find $P(x).$\n\n$P(x)=$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Since our quadratic polynomial has the double root ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=-4,$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=16,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})^{2} & =16{(x-(-4))}^{2} \\\\  & =16(x+4)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}16(x+4)^{2} & =16({x}^{2}+8x+16) \\\\  & =16{x}^{2}+128x+256.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=16{x}^{2}+128x+256.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278362 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1ee21c78-209f-564b-a005-86f58699a3be" :knowledge-point/title "Factoring a Quadratic Polynomial With Complex Roots"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "336bb7eb-a0a9-5f75-a472-668e4f091cd7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-(1+2\\text{i}))(x-(1-2\\text{i}))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278364} {:answer/id #uuid "ca3ff40b-3f47-5087-b7d3-5b0eff9368fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-(1+\\text{i}))^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278365} {:answer/id #uuid "f7caa5a0-9fb9-544d-a54a-d424d61a0a65" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-(2+\\text{i}))(x-(2-\\text{i}))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278366} {:answer/id #uuid "ab387316-d524-50fb-be1a-f59c07d27adc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-(1+\\text{i}))(x-(1-\\text{i}))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278367} {:answer/id #uuid "4fa62155-2320-5503-bb5b-05933f4c2c07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-(1-\\text{i}))^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278368}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ab387316-d524-50fb-be1a-f59c07d27adc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-(1+\\text{i}))(x-(1-\\text{i}))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278367} :answer-field/id #uuid "71596157-6620-5f49-b7f0-3a38727b166d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278363}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a03cbc43-a73d-597f-8992-1a873a7a2e15" :question/math-academy-id "q-46451" :question/problem "Factor ${x}^{2}-2x+2.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we let $f(x)={x}^{2}-2x+2.$\n\nNext, we solve $f(x)=0$ by completing the square, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-2x+2 & =0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-2\\cdot 1\\cdot x+{1}^{2})-{1}^{2}+2 & =0 \\\\ (x-1)^{2}-1+2 & =0 \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+1 & =0 \\\\ (x-1)^{2} & =-1 \\\\ (x-1)^{2} & ={\\text{i}}^{2} \\\\ x-1 & =\\pm \\text{i} \\\\ x & =1\\pm \\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since our quadratic equation has roots ${x}_{1}=1+\\text{i}$ and ${x}_{2}=1-\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=1,$ the expression ${x}^{2}-2x+2$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-2x+2 & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2}) \\\\  & =(x-(1+\\text{i}))(x-(1-\\text{i})).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278369 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b2478305-485c-53a6-9d6c-a72e0764dd4e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Quadratic Polynomial Given Two Real Roots and a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c9c9e5e-7dbf-5a7a-9563-c6919011e447" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3{t}^{2}+6t-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278371} {:answer/id #uuid "91492fe1-593b-5116-800a-fa725c9871d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3{t}^{2}-24t-24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278372} {:answer/id #uuid "4d927956-3793-5646-a27f-2df91a3d9eea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3{t}^{2}+18t-24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278373} {:answer/id #uuid "9c11fd91-6a87-5267-bfdf-5019faca7722" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3{t}^{2}+18t+24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278374} {:answer/id #uuid "0ffb8fca-2e9f-5905-9947-66dd4660264a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3{t}^{2}-6t+8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278375}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4d927956-3793-5646-a27f-2df91a3d9eea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3{t}^{2}+18t-24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278373} :answer-field/id #uuid "92ef6ad4-e62d-510b-981f-f55264ff5c34" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278370}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "25c39bba-bfc2-5bc7-ae64-8a07493fe9b7" :question/math-academy-id "q-46575" :question/problem "The quadratic polynomial $P(t)$ has roots ${t}_{1}=4,{t}_{2}=2,$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $-3.$ Find $P(t).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our quadratic polynomial has roots ${t}_{1}=4$ and ${t}_{2}=2,$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=-3,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t-{t}_{1})(t-{t}_{2}) & =(-3)(t-4)(t-2) \\\\  & =(-3)(t-4)(t-2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-3)(t-4)(t-2) & =(-3)({t}^{2}-6t+8) \\\\  & =-3{t}^{2}+18t-24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(t)=-3{t}^{2}+18t-24.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083631 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b2478305-485c-53a6-9d6c-a72e0764dd4e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Quadratic Polynomial Given Two Real Roots and a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a6c9b64a-3bc4-54b6-868d-6179537f56c0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2t^{2} - 7t + 12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186081153} {:answer/id #uuid "d39ea4f0-cf0d-524c-a652-94ce204ae8db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2t^{2} - 14t + 24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186081154} {:answer/id #uuid "fa7afcf9-b1f3-517e-8d24-24f6ac90acd0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t^{2} + 14t + 24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186081155} {:answer/id #uuid "13d98ff5-baa9-5431-a0f3-2dc6780b202f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2t^{2} + 24t - 14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186081156} {:answer/id #uuid "77ccf0f1-38b4-54c6-af7f-4deee1a40aa3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t^{2} + 7t - 12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186081157}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d39ea4f0-cf0d-524c-a652-94ce204ae8db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2t^{2} - 14t + 24" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186081154} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a47a18b-eae1-5cb3-adfd-49ad044edac7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186081152}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d5c335ce-d488-5146-97d2-7205e1322b91" :question/math-academy-id "q-46580" :question/problem "The quadratic polynomial $P(t)$ has roots ${t}_{1}=4,{t}_{2}=3,$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $2.$ Find $P(t).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our quadratic polynomial has roots ${t}_{1}=4$ and ${t}_{2}=3,$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=2,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t-{t}_{1})(t-{t}_{2}) & =(2)(t-4)(t-3) \\\\  & =2(t-4)(t-3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(t-4)(t-3) & =2({t}^{2}-7t+12) \\\\  & =2{t}^{2}-14t+24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(t)=2{t}^{2}-14t+24.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278376 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b2478305-485c-53a6-9d6c-a72e0764dd4e" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Quadratic Polynomial Given Two Real Roots and a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29ded292-e43d-5075-97af-34f7facd30cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{t}^{2}-25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278378} {:answer/id #uuid "adc560a8-d8cc-52bf-92d5-48f186f0f0e4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{t}^{2}+25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278379} {:answer/id #uuid "29406218-a3ab-5a3d-aa31-86d7be8fa8d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{t}^{2}+100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278380} {:answer/id #uuid "a8639525-0ea8-5cbf-aef8-ad0a2e3bd8c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{t}^{2}-25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278381} {:answer/id #uuid "999cd701-e40f-5cdd-a5ab-2f817fe10c32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{t}^{2}-100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278382}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "999cd701-e40f-5cdd-a5ab-2f817fe10c32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{t}^{2}-100" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278382} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ce6bc97-0f98-5b83-890b-a39073fb62c5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278377}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6f5c2009-ced1-5a8c-bd1c-b25716f3937a" :question/math-academy-id "q-46582" :question/problem "The quadratic polynomial $P(t)$ has roots ${t}_{1}=-5,{t}_{2}=5,$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $4.$ Find $P(t).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our quadratic polynomial has roots ${t}_{1}=-5$ and ${t}_{2}=5,$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=4,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(t-{t}_{1})(t-{t}_{2}) & =(4)(t-(-5))(t-5) \\\\  & =4(t+5)(t-5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(t+5)(t-5) & =4({t}^{2}-25) \\\\  & =4{t}^{2}-100.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(t)=4{t}^{2}-100.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278383 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b0262c8-c029-5a72-846b-1b4f4f3306ba" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Quadratic Polynomial Given a Double Root and a Leading Coefficient"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "be229dfa-2c74-5937-b172-229756cb25ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{y}^{2}+10y-50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278385} {:answer/id #uuid "fab60a97-529a-5f49-8208-14e5d5ac3666" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{y}^{2}+20y+50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278386} {:answer/id #uuid "a32ccf9e-7e25-55de-a415-8f564bafaa04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{y}^{2}-20y-50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278387} {:answer/id #uuid "79d3e4f6-c1f1-5dd5-a3a1-21c041d5f238" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{y}^{2}-10y+50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278388} {:answer/id #uuid "269e768f-cc4a-51e8-94c2-208d91e75570" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{y}^{2}+20y-50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278389}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a32ccf9e-7e25-55de-a415-8f564bafaa04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{y}^{2}-20y-50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278387} :answer-field/id #uuid "8fffbd29-bec8-58a3-94fb-50ac24c53a03" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278384}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1ccc0604-a69e-5d71-a18b-0a7af8ee586a" :question/math-academy-id "q-46590" :question/problem "The quadratic polynomial $P(y)$ has the double root ${y}_{1}={y}_{2}=-5,$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=-2.$ Find $P(y).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our quadratic polynomial has the double root ${y}_{1}={y}_{2}=-5,$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=-2,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(y-{y}_{1})^{2} & =(-2){(y-(-5))}^{2} \\\\  & =(-2){(y+5)}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-2){(y+5)}^{2} & =(-2)({y}^{2}+10y+25) \\\\  & =-2{y}^{2}-20y-50.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(y)=-2{y}^{2}-20y-50.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278390 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "70c149d8-3739-564c-97c5-6636860ad0c4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Quadratic Polynomial Given Two Imaginary or Complex Roots"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22b0bb66-ab2a-5a27-af14-2a0a0dbada61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{z}^{2}-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278392} {:answer/id #uuid "0e25af3c-27f9-5205-a41f-4c3bbfca749d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{z}^{2}+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278393} {:answer/id #uuid "2c03922d-a364-5bb2-980a-2ab035218047" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{z}^{2}-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278394} {:answer/id #uuid "2650b60f-b19f-5980-811b-db11bd19e60d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{z}^{2}+2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278395} {:answer/id #uuid "97fc9d72-6f45-5223-95e4-e835af2ae7cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{z}^{2}+4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278396}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "97fc9d72-6f45-5223-95e4-e835af2ae7cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{z}^{2}+4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278396} :answer-field/id #uuid "03190460-1db9-50a6-8b3d-1303c0b22c90" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278391}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1531518c-9671-50f9-8c99-70bc75711080" :question/math-academy-id "q-46594" :question/problem "The quadratic polynomial $f(z)$ has real coefficients, has roots ${z}_{1}=2\\text{i}$ and ${z}_{2}=-2\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $1.$ Find $f(z).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our quadratic polynomial has roots ${z}_{1}=2\\text{i}$ and ${z}_{2}=-2\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=1,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(z-{z}_{1})(z-{z}_{2}) & =(1)(z-2\\text{i})(z-(-2\\text{i})) \\\\  & =(z-2\\text{i})(z+2\\text{i})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(z-2\\text{i})(z+2\\text{i}) & ={z}^{2}-(2\\text{i})^{2} \\\\  & ={z}^{2}-4{\\text{i}}^{2} \\\\  & ={z}^{2}+4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(z)={z}^{2}+4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083634 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "70c149d8-3739-564c-97c5-6636860ad0c4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Quadratic Polynomial Given Two Imaginary or Complex Roots"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9dc49521-460b-5e7d-a718-28935c6850d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-z^{2} + 16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186081171} {:answer/id #uuid "ce20a156-d2ae-57d1-89ba-3b818c45c989" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-z^{2} - 8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186081172} {:answer/id #uuid "2fb15c98-776e-5009-892f-2b7d67bd15a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-z^{2} - 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186081173} {:answer/id #uuid "69f3a2ee-079e-50e2-990e-1db4ff34c95c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-z^{2} - 16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186081174} {:answer/id #uuid "745377a3-4d02-571c-b5bd-18ade077a60d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-z^{2} + 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186081175}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "69f3a2ee-079e-50e2-990e-1db4ff34c95c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-z^{2} - 16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186081174} :answer-field/id #uuid "d12a26d7-69f5-5239-bdb4-82a91ce2f3d4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186081170}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "abcce189-d2cf-555c-8ab7-44bd8cfd66d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-46596" :question/problem "The quadratic polynomial $f(z)$ has real coefficients, has roots ${z}_{1}=4\\text{i}$ and ${z}_{2}=-4\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $-1.$ Find $f(z).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our quadratic polynomial has roots ${z}_{1}=4\\text{i}$ and ${z}_{2}=-4\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=-1,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(z-{z}_{1})(z-{z}_{2}) & =(-1)(z-4\\text{i})(z-(-4\\text{i})) \\\\  & =-(z-4\\text{i})(z+4\\text{i})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-(z-4\\text{i})(z+4\\text{i}) & =-({z}^{2}-(4\\text{i})^{2}) \\\\  & =-({z}^{2}-16{\\text{i}}^{2}) \\\\  & =-({z}^{2}+16) \\\\  & =-{z}^{2}-16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(z)=-{z}^{2}-16.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278397 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "70c149d8-3739-564c-97c5-6636860ad0c4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Quadratic Polynomial Given Two Imaginary or Complex Roots"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "847cabab-85db-52b5-8a6b-9fd045a40178" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{y}^{2}+16y-34" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278399} {:answer/id #uuid "f54bf2a1-8f92-5506-9e35-19b483461718" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{y}^{2}+8y-17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278400} {:answer/id #uuid "e7b2f0a9-efcd-5eea-b7ec-e0afe92d945b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{y}^{2}-8y+17" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278401} {:answer/id #uuid "df104dba-92c2-5910-90d1-d082b9379f5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{y}^{2}-12y+16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278402} {:answer/id #uuid "551ae8e6-ad9b-56f2-804e-97263c4a63dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{y}^{2}-16y+34" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278403}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "551ae8e6-ad9b-56f2-804e-97263c4a63dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{y}^{2}-16y+34" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278403} :answer-field/id #uuid "aeebcfec-5091-5d94-9ace-ab6ed40d7c6a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278398}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cd86c63d-0bf3-584f-8641-fd4192baa1b8" :question/math-academy-id "q-46643" :question/problem "The quadratic polynomial $f(y)$ has real coefficients, has roots ${y}_{1}=4+\\text{i}$ and ${y}_{2}=4-\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $2.$ Find $f(y).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our quadratic polynomial has roots ${y}_{1}=4+\\text{i}$ and ${y}_{2}=4-\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=2,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(y-{y}_{1})(y-{y}_{2}) & =2(y-(4+\\text{i}))(y-(4-\\text{i}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(y-(4+\\text{i}))(y-(4-\\text{i})) & =2({y}^{2}-(4+\\text{i})y-(4-\\text{i})y+(4+\\text{i})(4-\\text{i})) \\\\  & =2({y}^{2}-(4+\\text{i}+4-\\text{i})y+({4}^{2}-{\\text{i}}^{2})) \\\\  & =2({y}^{2}-8y+(16+1)) \\\\  & =2{y}^{2}-16y+34.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(y)=2{y}^{2}-16y+34.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278404 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "70c149d8-3739-564c-97c5-6636860ad0c4" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Quadratic Polynomial Given Two Imaginary or Complex Roots"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01cee8da-4989-5c98-9f38-25611a052d70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{z}^{2}+12z-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278406} {:answer/id #uuid "834877a3-4d9c-5e2f-b3c6-bfb30ee49dff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{z}^{2}+12z-26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278407} {:answer/id #uuid "6ecd5e1e-bcd9-528c-8db8-89357eb0b511" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{z}^{2}+6z-13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278408} {:answer/id #uuid "f96dc97a-7ae4-53fd-81d4-79b04fa31120" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{z}^{2}-6z+9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278409} {:answer/id #uuid "3be52e73-35e6-5f96-baf8-8c8d3dc9b8dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{z}^{2}-12z-13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278410}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "834877a3-4d9c-5e2f-b3c6-bfb30ee49dff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{z}^{2}+12z-26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278407} :answer-field/id #uuid "7cced0f7-018b-50e6-8198-66207ebedcbf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278405}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b2b41d84-5bdc-5407-b7e8-a6afaca4585d" :question/math-academy-id "q-46664" :question/problem "The quadratic polynomial $f(z)$ has real coefficients, has roots ${z}_{1}=3+2\\text{i}$ and ${z}_{2}=3-2\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $-2.$ Find $f(z).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our quadratic polynomial has roots ${z}_{1}=3+2\\text{i}$ and ${z}_{2}=3-2\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=-2,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(z-{z}_{1})(z-{z}_{2}) & =(-2)(z-(3+2\\text{i}))(z-(3-2\\text{i}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-2)(z-(3+2\\text{i}))(z-(3-2\\text{i})) & =(-2)({z}^{2}-(3+2\\text{i})z-(3-2\\text{i})z+(3+2\\text{i})(3-2\\text{i})) \\\\  & =(-2)({z}^{2}-(3+2\\text{i}+3-2\\text{i})z+({3}^{2}-{2}^{2}{\\text{i}}^{2})) \\\\  & =(-2)({z}^{2}-6z+(9+4)) \\\\  & =-2{z}^{2}+12z-26.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(z)=-2{z}^{2}+12z-26.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278411 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1ee21c78-209f-564b-a005-86f58699a3be" :knowledge-point/title "Factoring a Quadratic Polynomial With Complex Roots"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fad84a9f-7290-5d5f-971f-3e5e1e0b7a16" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "v-(3-6\\text{i})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278413} {:answer/id #uuid "c7f8a2ac-f699-5021-8617-9d93ad04b0c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "v-(6-3\\text{i})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278414} {:answer/id #uuid "b1d898cb-d72a-58b7-8074-51dedad34dde" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "v-(2-6\\text{i})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278415} {:answer/id #uuid "bc3e76f7-aa5e-5ba9-b0a9-8fdcd4753b62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "v-(6+2\\text{i})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278416} {:answer/id #uuid "d1d26f0c-9ed5-571c-9ccb-2c77d604a666" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "v-(-6+3\\text{i})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278417}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c7f8a2ac-f699-5021-8617-9d93ad04b0c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "v-(6-3\\text{i})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278414} :answer-field/id #uuid "9b0861cd-13d3-5f77-84e3-b00c97a3ed3d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278412}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3374f4ce-1952-5ad1-8bea-6193ae4858d5" :question/math-academy-id "q-46670" :question/problem "Which of the following is a factor of $-{v}^{2}+12v-45?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we let $f(v)=-{v}^{2}+12v-45.$\n\nNext, we solve $f(v)=0$ by completing the square, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(v) & =0 \\\\ -{v}^{2}+12v-45 & =0 \\\\ {v}^{2}-12v+45 & =0 \\\\ ({v}^{2}-2\\cdot 6\\cdot v+{6}^{2})-{6}^{2}+45 & =0 \\\\ (v-6)^{2}-36+45 & =0 \\\\ (v-6)^{2}+9 & =0 \\\\ (v-6)^{2} & =-9 \\\\ (v-6)^{2} & =9{\\text{i}}^{2} \\\\ (v-6)^{2} & =(3\\text{i})^{2} \\\\ v-6 & =\\pm 3\\text{i} \\\\ v & =6\\pm 3\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince our quadratic equation has roots ${v}_{1}=6+3\\text{i}$ and ${v}_{2}=6-3\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=-1,$ the expression $-{v}^{2}+12v-45$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-{v}^{2}+12v-45 & =a(v-{v}_{1})(v-{v}_{2}) \\\\  & =-(v-(6+3\\text{i}))(v-(6-3\\text{i})).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, among the given options, only $v-(6-3\\text{i})$ is a factor of $-{v}^{2}+12v-45.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278418 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1ee21c78-209f-564b-a005-86f58699a3be" :knowledge-point/title "Factoring a Quadratic Polynomial With Complex Roots"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b5f3f1fb-b085-59ab-8672-5ce1df5683b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3(x-(2+3\\text{i}))(x-(2-3\\text{i}))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278420} {:answer/id #uuid "ef55662c-fef4-5517-bcf5-adc6cb4a82e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3(x-(1+4\\text{i}))(x-(1-4\\text{i}))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278421} {:answer/id #uuid "104a8a1d-914f-5fec-a54c-1b42dd75a6a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3(x-(1-4\\text{i}))^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278422} {:answer/id #uuid "0d564a8f-0bad-5830-9e33-207ab0e9a989" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-(2+4\\text{i}))(x-(2-4\\text{i}))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278423} {:answer/id #uuid "0f8aadcf-1d49-56f0-8793-46fc6c7b171e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-(2+3\\text{i}))^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278424}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ef55662c-fef4-5517-bcf5-adc6cb4a82e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3(x-(1+4\\text{i}))(x-(1-4\\text{i}))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278421} :answer-field/id #uuid "4dbd820d-7173-55ae-845d-fb82e878812d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278419}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "01b29fe9-9e4f-5dce-9d74-0d46f38589ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-46672" :question/problem "Factor $3{x}^{2}-6x+51.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we let $f(x)=3{x}^{2}-6x+51.$\n\nNext, we solve $f(x)=0$ by completing the square, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =0 \\\\ 3{x}^{2}-6x+51 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-2x+17 & =0 \\\\ ({x}^{2}-2\\cdot 1\\cdot x+{1}^{2})-{1}^{2}+17 & =0 \\\\ (x-1)^{2}-1+17 & =0 \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+16 & =0 \\\\ (x-1)^{2} & =-16 \\\\ (x-1)^{2} & =16{\\text{i}}^{2} \\\\ (x-1)^{2} & =(4\\text{i})^{2} \\\\ x-1 & =\\pm 4\\text{i} \\\\ x & =1\\pm 4\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since our quadratic equation has roots ${x}_{1}=1+4\\text{i}$ and ${x}_{2}=1-4\\text{i},$ and the coefficient of the quadratic term is $a=3,$ the expression $3{x}^{2}-6x+51$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}-6x+51 & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2}) \\\\  & =3(x-(1+4\\text{i}))(x-(1-4\\text{i})).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
